I've fixed #1119 and committed it as f1eb6731. Format check, clippy with -D warnings, build and the full test suite all pass, with no failures.

The test. every_provider_default_has_a_preset_or_a_stated_reason goes through KNOWN_PROVIDERS and checks each default with runs_on_guessed_limits, the same check that decides whether the guessed-limits warning fires. So the test and the warning can't disagree about what "has a preset" means. A provider passes only if its default has a preset, or if it has a row in DEFAULT_WITHOUT_PRESET with a reason. The check also runs the other way: a row for a provider that has since gained a preset fails, so a written reason can't go stale. I ran both checks once each, temporarily breaking the code and then restoring it in one command, with a NEUTERED marker in place while it was broken:
• Setting xai's default back to grok-4 failed with "xai: default 'grok-4' has no preset and no stated reason".
• Adding a stale xai row failed with "now has a preset; drop its DEFAULT_WITHOUT_PRESET row".

The defaults (prices per million tokens in/out):

| provider | old → new | price old → new | why |
|---|---|---|---|
| xai | grok-4 → grok-4.7 | $3/$15 (estimated) → $2/$6 | Cheaper, and real limits: 500K context, 64K output instead of a guessed 4096 output |
| mistral | mistral-large-latest → mistral-large-4 | $0.50/$1.50 → $0.70/$2.10 | Costs more and is still a preview model. But 4096 output tokens cuts a coding agent's file writes short, and Mistral lists Large 3 as deprecated with Large 4 as its replacement |
| zai | glm-4-plus → glm-5.3 | $0.70/$0.70 → $1.40/$4.40 | Output costs about 6× more. But the old default ran on guessed limits and isn't on Z.ai's pricing page at all, so it may no longer be served. The comment names glm-5.3-flash ($0.15/$0.50) as the cheap option |
| openrouter | kept | — | I rewrote the comment. Having a preset no longer sets sonnet-5.5 apart from sonnet-4.6 (#1116), so the reason that still holds is price: $2/$10 against $3/$15 |
| groq, cerebras, minimax, github | kept | — | yoagent ships no preset for any of their models. The reason is written next to each one, and they still show the guessed-limits warning |
| ollama, custom | kept | — | You run these servers yourself, so the limits come from your server |

Anyone with provider = "xai", "mistral" or "zai" and no model set will be moved to the new model without any notice. The old models still work with --model. The code comments and the commit message both say this.

Checks on the real binary: I ran it from a clean temp directory so this repo's .yoyo.toml wouldn't fill in a model. The three new defaults ran with no guessed-limits warning, and groq still warned. The existing warning test in model_limits_note.rs listed 7 providers whose defaults trip the warning; it now lists 4, exactly the three I fixed taken out.

Outside the task's file list:
• I edited the warning test in model_limits_note.rs, which the task allowed as one extra test file.
• The docs default tables in models.md, installation.md and fork.md were already wrong before this change: xai said grok-3, deepseek said deepseek-chat instead of deepseek-v4-pro, and fork.md showed an old Sonnet 4 for openrouter. I fixed all of those rows along with the three moved defaults.
• I also added glm-5.3 to zai's list of known models, then took it out again: that list already includes every model yoagent has a preset for.
